==Battleground==
*The enemy base here is a [[Moai Statue (Enemy Base)|Moai Statue]].
*Infinite [[Fireworks Guys (High-Yield)]] spawn, delay 6~12 seconds<sup>180f~360f</sup>.
*Infinite [[Fireworks Guys (Low-Yield)]] spawn after 4 seconds<sup>120f</sup>, delay 6~12 seconds<sup>180f~360f</sup>.
*1 [[Easter B.B.Bunny]] spawns after 10 seconds<sup>300f</sup>.
*1 [[Gold Hippoe]] spawns after 13.33 seconds<sup>400f</sup>.
*When the base reaches 99% HP:
**1 [[Pigge Victorious]] spawns.
**2 [[Easter B.B.Bunny|Easter B.B.Bunnies]] spawn, delay 16.67 seconds<sup>500f</sup>.
**1 [[Gold Hippoe]] spawns.
*When the base reaches 50% HP:
**3 [[Gary Gory|Gary Gories]] spawn, delay 16.67 seconds<sup>500f</sup>.
**3 [[Pigge Victorious|Pigge Victoriouses]] spawn, delay 20 seconds<sup>600f</sup>.
**3 [[Easter B.B.Bunny|Easter B.B.Bunnies]] spawn, delay 16.67 seconds<sup>500f</sup>.

==Strategy==
Use [[Hip Hop Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Can Can Cat]] or a similar melee unit to stall the beginning enemies for money as they safely out-range the beginning peons. [[Tank Cat (Normal Cat)|Dual]] [[Crazed Tank Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Erasers]] should cover meatshielding and prevent Can Can from wasting an attack on a Firework Guy. When you hit the base, start spawning your [[:Category:Area Attack Cats|Area Attackers]]. Some good examples include [[Courier Cat]], [[Cyborg Cat]], and [[Drama Cats]], but anything with melee range and decent DPS should work. Pigge Victorious has much more range than the rest of the enemies here, but [[Crazed Gross Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Crazed]]/[[Brainwashed Gross Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Brainwashed]] Gross can quickly snipe them using the other enemies as a stepping stone, but those units aren't needed at all to beat the stage. The Moai Statue is arguably the most threatening enemy here, but bulky units can just absorb the damage and hit the base anyway.

